    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T2H1N5C4",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-OR copy 4 of stage 2: Y = NAND(A2, B2), feeding T2H1CARRYC4.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_d951d6318e92413d98e15f476e11f31b",
        "IdGuid": "113cb1df-e3ef-4ad5-adeb-f26594ae6d4d",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "7dcc9cca-3fc3-4c9b-8015-81b9b9cd6ae9",
          "a2ecd5d7-360e-4213-a2a9-7b24379fd83e",
          "1fc7ae09-0cd7-49c5-898d-113062bc550c",
